 "notes": "Fig. 2 of the paper: 95% C.L. upper limit on the neutron-nucleon monopole-dipole (scalar-pseudoscalar) coupling |g_S^N g_P^n| vs interaction range lambda (10^6-10^14 m), derived from Lorentz/CPT-violation comagnetometer data with the Sun and Moon as sources. Reported curve is the boundary of the dark-grey region excluded by this work: the envelope of the two solid lines (Moon curve for lambda < ~10^10.3 m, Sun curve at larger lambda). Curves extracted from PDF vector paths; axis calibration verified against the quoted asymptote |g_S g_P| < 1.6e-35 for lambda > 10^12 m and against the analytic form (1+R/lambda)exp(-R/lambda) (agreement < 0.01 dex). Range converted to mass via m = 1.97e-7 eV.m / lambda (matches the figure's top mass axis). Curves clipped at the figure frame top (10^-25) at the high-mass end. Not a dark-matter limit; no density assumed.",
